    <heading level="1">Real-World Applications</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, write the polynomial function that models the given situation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="75" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A rectangle has a length of 10 units and a width of 8 units. Squares of $$x$$ by $$x$$ units are cut out of each corner, and then the sides are folded up to create an open box. Express the volume of the box as a polynomial function in terms of $$x.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f(x)=4 x 3 -36 x 2 +80x f(x)=4 x 3 -36 x 2 +80x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="76" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider the same rectangle of the preceding problem. Squares of $$2x$$ by $$2x$$ units are cut out of each corner. Express the volume of the box as a polynomial in terms of $$x.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="77" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A square has sides of 12 units. Squares $$x + 1$$ by $$x + 1$$ units are cut out of each corner, and then the sides are folded up to create an open box. Express the volume of the box as a function in terms of $$x.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f(x)=4 x 3 -36 x 2 +60x+100 f(x)=4 x 3 -36 x 2 +60x+100$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="78" has_solution="false">
